# The frozen integrity zome.
#
# A circle IS the hash of this compiled wasm. Change the source — including a
# comment, which was measured to change it — and every circle anybody has ever
# made becomes unreachable. Their records stay on their own disks and no build
# of this app will ever show them again, with no error anywhere.
#
# So the wasm hash is pinned here and CI fails if it moves. See the README, and
# docs/to-a-product.md for what to do if it genuinely has to change (short
# answer: that is a migration with everybody re-invited, not a commit).
#
# Frozen 2026-09-08, at release v0.1.0.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠️  THE TWO PLATFORMS DO NOT AGREE, AND THIS IS A BUG (found 2026-09-08)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Identical source. Identical pinned compiler (rustc 1.98.0, per
# rust-toolchain.toml). Different wasm:
#
#   Windows  dd942cac…      the machine the released installer is built on
#   Linux    7ca250f3…      GitHub Actions, and anybody building from source
#
# Different wasm means a different DNA hash means **a different network**. So a
# circle made in the published Windows installer and a circle made from a
# Linux build are not the same circle, and their members can never find each
# other — silently, as always.
#
# The README currently tells Linux and macOS users to build from source. Taken
# together with the above, that instruction hands them an app that cannot talk
# to any Windows user. That is not a theory; it is what these two lines say.
#
# The likely cause is source paths embedded in panic and debug strings —
# C:\Users\user\… against /home/runner/… — which `--remap-path-prefix` exists
# to normalise. Not attempted yet, because fixing it changes the hash again and
# therefore the DNA of the release published today.
#
# See docs/to-a-product.md. Do not treat the freeze as settled until this is.

linux    7ca250f33f303395b44fb40bff2dc4cd74b5310841887e6e8b170d9398b5bab8
windows  dd942cacc54fa741677dc5128d0469ce22cb1a022206345f0f69e31d9a541de6
